  "description": "BUCMAO crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C8 H20 N1 O2 1+,C100 H200 Mn5 N8 Nd8 O64 1-,7(C2 H3 N1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd6 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd7 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd8 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 6 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn3 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn4 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn5 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.459-4.254 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.83-117.89°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C122H241Mn5N16Nd8O66. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 12 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 NO3 (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 4 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
